<title>UK: EBRD provides $50 million to Russia's Avtobank.</title>
<headline>EBRD provides $50 million to Russia's Avtobank.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Bank for Reconstruction and Development (EBRD) said it was providing a $50 million financing package to Russia's Avtobank.</p>
<p>The amount includes taking an eight-percent stake worth $20 million in the bank and a loan for the remaining amount.</p>
<p>&quot;(It) will enable Avtobank to strengthen its capital base and provide medium- and long-term funds for on-lending to private industrial enterprises,&quot; EBRD deputy vice-president David Hexter said.</p>
<p>Avtobank, among the 15 largest banks in Russia and operating in and around Moscow, also signed a $10 million trade facility with the EBRD.</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Thatcher, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7770 (fax +44 171 583 7239)</p>
